Z||000009||thomas_l||11-27-2001||02:08 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>I will sort out the racing list right now<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thank you! I normally avoid e-mail lists but this seemed to merit an exception   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.<P>Culture shock, eh? By the time you go back to Ontario you will be spoiled rotten by restaraunts on every corner, huge mega-grocery and discount stores, and cheap gasoline. Oh yeah - the best is going into a stop & rob for a soda or something and getting folding money back in change for $10. Long live the $1 bill!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Oh yeah I almost forgot. Something I dearly missed while visiting Canada: get to love the surly attitude that every store clerk and cashier you will meet here in the US. Remember - they are doing you a favor by being there to put up with your time-wasting, trivial request to spend money at their place of business.<p>[This message has been edited by thomas_l (edited 11-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||thomas_l||11-27-2001||02:11 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fformula88:<BR><B>You got target pegged about right!  Its an upscale department store like a K-Mart.  Not that upscale however.  Its more like a kmart would be if they cleaned their stores.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well... maybe clean their stores and stock merchandise that isn't just the absolutely cheapest made crap on the planet. I make an occaisional trip to K-mart just to get mad and remember why they suck so bad  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
